Subject:  Western apparently is as gutless as the rest!
Date: Fri, 3 Dec 1993 19:17:55 GMT
Message-ID: <1993Dec3.191755.29918@julian.uwo.ca>

Well it appears that the University of Western Ontario cannot even
follow its own policies regarding USENET carrying, I quote from the
CUC USENET CARRYING POLICY: (emphasis mine)

7. Policy Regarding Harmful or Illegal News Groups
If  it  can be demonstrated beyond a reasonable doubt that a certain news group
                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
consistently does direct and demonstrable harm to a person or persons, than  it
^^^^^^^^^^^^
should  be considered if action should be taken regarding that group.  The same
applies to a news group whose contents are obviously illegal.
                                           ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^

I DEMAND to be told about the CUC's decision to remove the newsgroup
alt.fan.karla-homolka. When was it made and how were the emphasized
phrases above reconcile?  The way I read this, it must be shown
`beyond a reasonable doubt' that the postings are `consistently' and
`obviously' illegal.  How was this determined? 

THIS IS A VERY SERIOUS BREACH OF THE POLICY AS STATED! You should be
as upset as I am about this censorshit, I do not believe we should
allow this to go on. The CUC is accountable for their actions, where 
is the reasoning for this action? Why was it not stated BEFORE action
was taken?  I WANT ANSWERS TO THESE QUESTIONS!


Funny, I was just saying to people yesterday how proud I was to be a
member of this university for their proper stand. Apparently I was
premature with my praise, and I hang my head in shame!

The full text of the CUC USENET CARRYING POLICY can be found via ftp

ftp julian.uwo.ca
login: ftp
passwd: <your-email-address>
cd pub/doc/usenet-policy
get 1991-11-27.cuc

There are a number of different documents there, all worth a good
read. I just wish ITS and the CUC would read them as well.

cheerskinch














